1
00:00:08,925 --> 00:00:10,927
<i>Urgent. We're moving to Plan B.</i>

2
00:00:12,178 --> 00:00:13,263
<i>I repeat. Plan B.</i>

3
00:00:16,057 --> 00:00:17,142
What's going on?

4
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:21,146
The situation got much worse.

5
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:23,166
Who are you?

6
00:01:24,084 --> 00:01:25,085
I...

7
00:01:25,627 --> 00:01:26,628
I'm...

8
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:32,717
I'm Senior Investigator.
At PSIA. Kasahara Reina.

9
00:01:34,719 --> 00:01:35,762
For how long?

10
00:01:37,847 --> 00:01:39,099
Since the beginning?

11
00:01:42,102 --> 00:01:43,770
To think I thought of us as family.

12
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:48,066
Having worked together all these years.

13
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:50,026
You...

14
00:01:51,861 --> 00:01:54,906
You betrayed your own compatriots.

15
00:01:56,491 --> 00:01:58,243
They became criminals for you.

16
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:01,830
They had nowhere else to go.

17
00:02:10,213 --> 00:02:11,422
Do it. Kill me.

18
00:02:17,512 --> 00:02:18,888
Seo Hyun-tae!

19
00:02:20,682 --> 00:02:21,683
Let her go.

20
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:25,270
I said, let her go.

21
00:02:29,107 --> 00:02:30,316
Yoon Soo-kyung.

22
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:33,611
The rest is on you now.

23
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:49,418
Ms. Kasahara. Wake up. Ms Kasahara.

24
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:51,295
No, no, please wake up, come on.

25
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:53,756
Soo-kyung. Call an ambulance.

26
00:02:56,676 --> 00:02:57,886
No, please.

27
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:49,520
Ito.

28
00:03:50,855 --> 00:03:52,565
Hey, Ito.

29
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:45,410
Hey, Ito!

30
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:52,583
Hey. Hey!

31
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:54,961
Hey, Ito!

32
00:04:58,381 --> 00:04:59,924
Why won't this thing move?

33
00:05:13,896 --> 00:05:15,940
What the... What's that?

34
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:24,032
<i>Guilinggao</i>. Only ten dollars.
Just ten dollars. <i>Guilinggao.</i>

35
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:27,326
Whoa.

36
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:28,661
Hey, man, are you drunk?

37
00:05:29,954 --> 00:05:30,997
Go check the machine.

38
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:13,414
Nice to see you.

39
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:15,958
How did you...

40
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:25,551
Yoon-Ok.

41
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:30,848
She's good. Isn't she?

42
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:27,113
THE BLUE ROAD

43
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:05,067
"One fear gives birth to endless fears,

44
00:08:06,986 --> 00:08:09,739
but its methods shall remain hidden."

45
00:08:16,954 --> 00:08:18,915
EMIRI'S TREATISE
ON MILITARY STRATEGY

46
00:08:23,002 --> 00:08:24,962
Wait, I think I know you.

47
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:27,798
You used to work with my father.

48
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:30,718
And you'll be taking care of us
from now on, right?

49
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:37,892
I'm told you're Mr. Minamoto's son.

50
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:39,560
Yeah?

51
00:08:40,853 --> 00:08:41,854
Yes, that's right.

52
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:43,606
My name's Emi Shunsuke.

53
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:47,610
Are you Korean?

54
00:08:48,402 --> 00:08:49,779
Or are you Japanese?

55
00:08:56,494 --> 00:08:57,495
You know,

56
00:08:58,454 --> 00:09:00,122
gotta say, I'm not really sure.

57
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:02,708
I never did find out.

58
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:08,756
<i>Ito Makoto.</i>

59
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:23,771
Mr. Seo Hyun-tae from an ANSP Print Shop.

60
00:09:34,991 --> 00:09:37,034
There's something
I should probably tell you.

61
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,502
Because of you, I'm not a cop anymore.

62
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:50,548
So you'd better give me a straight answer.

63
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:54,301
How did you know Hong Du-yeong?

64
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:55,386
Tell me.

65
00:09:57,013 --> 00:09:58,014
Hmm?

66
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:00,808
Did the ANSP kill him?

67
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:02,560
Did they torture him?

68
00:10:03,394 --> 00:10:05,479
I want to hear you say the words.

69
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:12,570
Not stopping till you break.

70
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:40,431
<i>How is she?</i>

71
00:10:44,393 --> 00:10:46,479
She's still comatose, but she's alive.

72
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:49,190
I'm glad she's okay.

73
00:10:52,777 --> 00:10:53,778
Here.

74
00:10:54,612 --> 00:10:57,073
- I found this GPS tracker on Ito's car.
- Okay.

75
00:10:59,241 --> 00:11:00,993
You guys planted it there, didn't you?

76
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:07,333
Kim Seok has kidnapped Seo Hyun-tae.

77
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:09,669
Huh?

78
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:11,419
Truth be told,

79
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:15,341
if we failed, our backup plan
was to just use Kim Seok instead.

80
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:19,679
Are you serious?

81
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:24,265
Because of you damn NIS people,

82
00:11:24,266 --> 00:11:26,976
he might kill Seo Hyun-tae
with his bare hands.

83
00:11:26,977 --> 00:11:29,020
- Listen.
- No, no. Save it.

84
00:11:29,021 --> 00:11:31,857
Where is he right now?
Don't pretend you don't know.

85
00:11:33,442 --> 00:11:34,568
Well?

86
00:11:38,406 --> 00:11:39,407
Answer me.

87
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:42,034
Kowloon Mansions.

88
00:11:42,618 --> 00:11:45,370
It's a building where
undocumented immigrants tend to live.

89
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:47,665
They were seen on CCTV heading there.

90
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:49,917
But please don't worry about it.

91
00:11:50,584 --> 00:11:52,961
Once the Hong Kong police arrive...

92
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:55,256
Where are you going?
We have to do this together.

93
00:11:59,719 --> 00:12:03,681
Kim Seok and I
may not have worked together long,

94
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:06,559
but we've been through some stuff,
you know?

95
00:12:08,894 --> 00:12:10,396
You get what I'm saying?

96
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:13,858
Wait.

97
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:26,245
All right.

98
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,789
Let's go through this step by step.

99
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:32,084
First up, the print shop.

100
00:12:36,005 --> 00:12:40,134
It was an Anti-Communist Investigation
Office run by the ANSP for interrogations.

101
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:42,636
Right?

102
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,364
Is that right?

103
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:06,035
Yes.

104
00:13:07,703 --> 00:13:08,828
You're right.

105
00:13:08,829 --> 00:13:10,372
Next.

106
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:12,458
The original.

107
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:14,668
Using methods...

108
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:18,379
that were designed by the ANSP.

109
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:21,425
Breaking bones, twisting limbs.
And you were a member, weren't you?

110
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:23,803
The Minamoto family employs you.

111
00:13:47,409 --> 00:13:49,328
Nobody. Nobody.

112
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:52,581
Nobody designed it.

113
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:56,335
We never saw it coming.

114
00:14:05,469 --> 00:14:06,554
What do you mean?

115
00:14:07,596 --> 00:14:08,889
The methods were...

116
00:14:12,852 --> 00:14:14,019
accidental.

117
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:18,440
MUNHWA PRINTING COMPANY

118
00:14:18,941 --> 00:14:20,067
<i>The Print Shop.</i>

119
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:24,697
<i>An organization in the ANSP</i>

120
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:28,199
<i>made up of North Korean defectors,
Korean-Chinese people,</i>

121
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:29,617
<i>Koryo-saram...</i>

122
00:14:29,618 --> 00:14:31,328
<i>people who were undocumented.</i>

123
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:44,008
REPORT SPIES

124
00:14:48,846 --> 00:14:49,847
Huh.

125
00:14:57,354 --> 00:14:58,689
<i>Our main purpose</i>

126
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:01,525
<i>was to inflict illegal torture.</i>

127
00:15:04,361 --> 00:15:06,405
<i>We were trained in the art of torture.</i>

128
00:15:07,823 --> 00:15:11,076
<i>Our chief had a strong fixation
on the anti-Japanese movement.</i>

129
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:18,167
<i>He came from a Japanese family that had
remained in Korea after its liberation.</i>

130
00:15:20,336 --> 00:15:22,463
<i>His Korean name was Won Seung-il.</i>

131
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,675
<i>His Japanese name was Minamoto Shoichi.</i>

132
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:34,016
<i>Later, he would go on
to build Minamoto Pharmaceuticals.</i>

133
00:15:37,102 --> 00:15:38,187
<i>The methods he used...</i>

134
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:43,442
You can stop this, you know?

135
00:15:45,569 --> 00:15:46,987
I know how hard it is.

136
00:15:48,197 --> 00:15:49,448
I can see your pain.

137
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:52,368
Come on, enough.

138
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:54,994
I'm telling you.

139
00:15:54,995 --> 00:15:56,497
I have no idea.

140
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:03,587
If that's the case, what's this here? Huh?

141
00:16:05,464 --> 00:16:08,174
Japan has destroyed Korea's spirit.

142
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:11,804
Japanese collaborators
have made a mockery of our citizens.

143
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:18,227
Do you not know the President's policy?

144
00:16:20,729 --> 00:16:22,982
Please. Sir.

145
00:16:24,608 --> 00:16:26,068
Please, I have a family.

146
00:16:26,777 --> 00:16:28,654
I have a wife, I'm begging you.

147
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:33,575
I've got a boy. He needs me, please.
He needs his father, please.

148
00:16:34,451 --> 00:16:37,538
Sir, please. Please, have mercy.

149
00:16:39,707 --> 00:16:41,041
I'm begging you.

150
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:56,265
All right.

151
00:16:57,975 --> 00:16:59,059
Enough, I get it.

152
00:16:59,643 --> 00:17:00,894
Man.

153
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:11,238
Hey. Hey. Get back here.

154
00:17:12,614 --> 00:17:13,990
Stop. Wait.

155
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:15,074
Come back here.

156
00:17:15,075 --> 00:17:16,535
Hey, that's a dead end.

157
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:18,078
Son of a bitch.

158
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:21,707
- Get back here.
- Get away.

159
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:24,417
There's no way out.

160
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:25,544
Stop.

161
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:27,170
Look, I get it, okay?

162
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:28,630
No, no, stop.

163
00:17:43,562 --> 00:17:45,022
<i>That was the first time.</i>

164
00:17:46,273 --> 00:17:47,274
<i>We...</i>

165
00:17:48,108 --> 00:17:49,651
<i>We had to get rid of the body.</i>

166
00:17:50,694 --> 00:17:53,947
<i>So, we burned off the fingerprints,</i>

167
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:56,116
<i>and twisted up his limbs.</i>

168
00:17:58,827 --> 00:18:00,496
<i>We twisted them even more.</i>

169
00:18:02,998 --> 00:18:04,166
And then we

170
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:07,503
threw the body into the sewer.

171
00:18:19,848 --> 00:18:21,433
We had the news report

172
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:25,187
that it was the work of a serial killer.

173
00:18:28,482 --> 00:18:30,025
So no one suspected us.

174
00:18:33,278 --> 00:18:34,279
You're saying

175
00:18:36,323 --> 00:18:38,158
Minamoto taught his men that method?

176
00:18:39,993 --> 00:18:40,994
That's right.

177
00:18:43,288 --> 00:18:47,042
And then, we kept on using it.

178
00:18:49,461 --> 00:18:51,755
It worked far better
than we could have imagined.

179
00:18:53,882 --> 00:18:56,218
If someone was killed during a protest,

180
00:18:58,345 --> 00:19:00,139
we'd dispose of the body that same way.

181
00:19:01,473 --> 00:19:03,308
We'd twist the limbs, and toss the corpse.

182
00:19:07,813 --> 00:19:09,648
And no one blamed the ANSP.

183
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:14,610
And if journalists sensationalized it
as a murder,

184
00:19:14,611 --> 00:19:16,572
you'd still benefit
from the fear it'd create.

185
00:19:17,072 --> 00:19:18,073
Exactly.

186
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:21,410
And so more were killed.

187
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:25,831
And more were dumped in the sewer.

188
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,294
More than I can even count.

189
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:35,382
But some were just left to rot.

190
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:39,011
One of them was Hong Du-yeong, right?

191
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,101
Kim Seok,

192
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:55,027
Hong Du-yeong worked with us.

193
00:19:57,321 --> 00:19:58,322
With you?

194
00:20:05,787 --> 00:20:07,539
He was one of us, you know?

195
00:20:18,425 --> 00:20:20,427
<i>He was our torture technician.</i>

196
00:20:35,901 --> 00:20:37,444
He was one of us.

197
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:45,535
He was one of us, kid.

198
00:20:59,466 --> 00:21:00,467
Bullshit.

199
00:21:00,968 --> 00:21:02,010
He was my senior.

200
00:21:04,596 --> 00:21:07,140
He was a real artist,
far better than I was.

201
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:10,143
- Hmm.
- I admired him. He was a master.

202
00:21:13,021 --> 00:21:14,815
He taught me everything I know.

203
00:21:15,482 --> 00:21:17,150
He was the best out of all of us.

204
00:21:18,068 --> 00:21:19,069
He was...

205
00:21:27,536 --> 00:21:29,329
Like I'd believe that bullshit.

206
00:21:31,581 --> 00:21:35,919
Human joints are as strong as ox sinew.

207
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:40,548
No matter how hard you twist,
they hold on.

208
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:41,967
You better shut your mouth.

209
00:21:42,467 --> 00:21:46,596
That's why you have to wrench them,
like you're ripping them apart

210
00:21:48,056 --> 00:21:49,474
to twist them properly.

211
00:21:52,894 --> 00:21:54,896
He taught me all about anatomy.

212
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:01,069
We had to dispose of so many bodies.

213
00:22:01,862 --> 00:22:03,946
Think of how many were never found.

214
00:22:03,947 --> 00:22:05,449
They only found four, right?

215
00:22:06,783 --> 00:22:07,784
Right?

216
00:22:12,831 --> 00:22:18,670
I guess I could tell you
everything about it now, huh?

217
00:22:27,846 --> 00:22:29,181
I'm warning you.

218
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:33,101
You don't wanna hear it?

219
00:22:34,227 --> 00:22:35,228
Stop it.

220
00:22:36,355 --> 00:22:37,606
Detective Kim.

221
00:22:43,862 --> 00:22:44,946
Detective Kim!

222
00:22:51,661 --> 00:22:53,497
Hey, Detective Kim!

223
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:56,375
If you're gonna kill me,

224
00:22:57,876 --> 00:22:59,169
you'd better do it now.

225
00:23:02,589 --> 00:23:03,632
You think I won't?

226
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:08,512
Do it.

227
00:23:13,558 --> 00:23:14,684
Kill me.

228
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,605
Hey! Kim Seok!

229
00:23:19,356 --> 00:23:20,399
Detective Kim!

230
00:23:21,149 --> 00:23:22,234
Stop. You're a cop.

231
00:23:23,485 --> 00:23:25,112
You're a police officer!

232
00:23:29,991 --> 00:23:31,159
Right, we're moving.

233
00:23:53,223 --> 00:23:54,224
Why?

234
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:56,601
I'm just being honest.

235
00:23:59,855 --> 00:24:01,106
Is it so hard to buy?

236
00:24:08,155 --> 00:24:09,156
How bout this, then?

237
00:24:13,493 --> 00:24:14,828
The <i>gukbap</i> place. Yeah?

238
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:25,672
You saw me.

239
00:24:32,387 --> 00:24:33,388
Wait a minute.

240
00:24:36,016 --> 00:24:37,017
Who is that?

241
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:39,102
Don't worry, he's just a friend.

242
00:24:40,228 --> 00:24:41,646
From the Blue Road.

243
00:24:43,523 --> 00:24:44,608
But who is he?

244
00:24:48,612 --> 00:24:51,739
My goodness, Hyun-tae.
It's been such a long time.

245
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:52,823
Hello.

246
00:24:52,824 --> 00:24:54,159
How have you been?

247
00:25:05,253 --> 00:25:06,630
<i>My uncle died that day.</i>

248
00:25:12,260 --> 00:25:13,470
So you do remember.

249
00:25:40,956 --> 00:25:41,957
Kim Seok!

250
00:25:42,832 --> 00:25:43,833
You in there?

251
00:25:45,043 --> 00:25:47,045
- Hey. Answer me.
- No. Inose, get out of here.

252
00:25:47,546 --> 00:25:49,214
- Get out!
- Detective.

253
00:26:24,874 --> 00:26:25,875
That all you got?

254
00:26:28,795 --> 00:26:30,171
That your best effort?

255
00:26:33,216 --> 00:26:34,884
Do you even wanna catch me?

256
00:27:28,355 --> 00:27:30,523
Kim Seok,

257
00:27:46,289 --> 00:27:47,290
Show me.

258
00:27:47,874 --> 00:27:49,042
Inose.

259
00:27:50,460 --> 00:27:53,128
It's okay. It's okay, Inose.

260
00:27:53,129 --> 00:27:54,964
It's not that bad. You're okay.

261
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:57,800
Inose.

262
00:27:57,801 --> 00:27:58,927
Come on.

263
00:28:13,692 --> 00:28:14,693
Inose.

264
00:28:17,278 --> 00:28:18,279
No, come on.

265
00:28:38,800 --> 00:28:39,801
An ambulance.

266
00:28:42,262 --> 00:28:43,263
We need an ambulance,

267
00:28:50,562 --> 00:28:52,312
Call an ambulance now!

268
00:28:52,313 --> 00:28:53,606
Someone!

269
00:28:54,399 --> 00:28:56,608
Call an ambulance. Hurry!

270
00:28:56,609 --> 00:28:57,694
Hey.

271
00:29:00,447 --> 00:29:02,490
Inose. Inose.

272
00:29:42,572 --> 00:29:46,034
YOU DID GOOD, INOSE
